To add the NOOP and MODE client requests in the proper locations, we can place the NOOP command after the PASS command to keep the connection alive and the MODE command before the LIST command to set the transfer mode. Here’s the modified sequence of client requests:

```
USER anonymous
PASS ubuntu
NOOP
SYST
PWD
PORT 127,0,0,1,152,193
MODE S
LIST
QUIT
```

This sequence ensures that the NOOP command is sent right after authentication and before any data transfer commands, and the MODE command is set to Stream mode (S) before the LIST command is issued

